
h1 Authentication and API conventions

h2 Choose a credential
Credential | When to use it
Workspace API key | Connect an application to a workspace. Search Only permission allows reading and searching. Read / Write also allows adding and changing content.
User access token | Manage an account, organization, members, API keys, or billing after signing in. The user’s role determines which actions are allowed.
MCP connection | Let an AI assistant use the workspaces, drives, and actions you approve during sign-in.

h2 Make a workspace request
curl "$POLYGRES_BASE_URL/v1/sdk/context" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $POLYGRES_API_KEY"

h2 Repeat an operation

h2 Update a versioned resource
# Save the ETag returned by this read, then set DRIVE_ETAG to that exact value.
curl -i "$POLYGRES_BASE_URL/v1/drives/$DRIVE_ID" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $POLYGRES_API_KEY"
 
curl -X PATCH "$POLYGRES_BASE_URL/v1/drives/$DRIVE_ID" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $POLYGRES_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "If-Match: $DRIVE_ETAG" \
  -d '{"name":"Handbooks"}'

h2 Lists and errors
{
  "error": {
    "code": "invalid_credentials",
    "message": "Authentication failed. Provide a valid access token or API key.",
    "request_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
    "details": {}
  }
}